  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "qw39cKMDlNEb63FJUfzd9k6HY3jWT9Ma6rQUkRyfQWwveePCSpWaSP9053FGTG+PJItfAjxa84FBwpYNsKgnkQ==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 541291,
  "published": "2026-09-11T01:18:47.373Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- When the headers to look for are not all in one row, HeadersNotMatchingSameRowException is thrown. Its message names the workbook and the worksheet and says where each header was found, or that it was not found within the search limits.\n- It derives from InvalidOperationException, which is what this error was thrown as up to 1.0.2, so existing catch blocks keep working.\n- Reading a worksheet by name no longer replaces that message with a generic one.\n- Each worksheet looks for its headers from scratch. Until 1.0.2, when a header was missing from a later worksheet, that worksheet was read at the column the header had in the previous one, returning the wrong data without any error; now the missing header is reported.\n- A header that is not found is reported even when it is the only one; until 1.0.2 its worksheet was read anyway.\n- CustomColumnHeaderMatch runs its condition in every worksheet. Until 1.0.2 the header text it matched in the first worksheet replaced the condition, so later worksheets, and later reads with the same configuration, only found that exact text. The column keeps the name of the first header matched, so every worksheet's values come out under the same name, as before.",
